{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484210,"name":"Martin Holmes","username":"Martin_Holmes","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/9fc29f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:34:13.386Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy Grok Bot computer is unreachable again today, September 5, 2026.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is now a recurring failure on the same Grok Bot environment, not a first-time connectivity problem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExisting support ticket: T-F35990\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecent history:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe computer previously became unreachable and required Cursor backend repair.\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor restored the existing computer and synced data.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe problem subsequently returned.\u003cbr\u003e\nYesterday, September 4, Grok Bot was unavailable for most/all of the day.\u003cbr\u003e\nUpdate, Recover, and Reset all failed.\u003cbr\u003e\nI received the *.cursorvm.com connectivity error.\u003cbr\u003e\nI tested from a completely separate cellular hotspot and the same failure remained, making my normal home network an unlikely cause.\u003cbr\u003e\nI reported yesterday’s outage through this forum and support.\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot was eventually restored.\u003cbr\u003e\nToday the Grok Bot computer is unreachable again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am not going to run Update, Recover, or Reset again, because those procedures repeatedly failed during the previous incidents and the environment has already required backend intervention.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease escalate this directly for backend investigation/repair of the existing computer and investigate the underlying cause of these repeated failures rather than treating each outage as an isolated incident.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI rely on this environment for ongoing business workflows, and repeated day-long outages are making the service operationally unreliable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease preserve the existing environment, agents, conversations, and synced state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen my existing Grok Bot environment on Windows. Grok Bot attempts to connect to its existing cloud computer but cannot reach it. This same environment has repeatedly become unreachable and has previously required Cursor backend repair.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy existing Grok Bot cloud computer should remain continuously available and reconnect normally without requiring repeated backend repairs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.39.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484210-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484210-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T19:34:22.178Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":0.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170722,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-computer-unreachable-again-recurring-backend-failure-after-multiple-repairs","display_username":"Martin Holmes","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136225,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-computer-unreachable-again-recurring-backend-failure-after-multiple-repairs/170722/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false}],"stream":[484210]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"},{"id":373,"name":"computer-use","slug":"computer-use"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot computer unreachable AGAIN — recurring backend failure after multiple repairs","id":170722,"title":"Grok Bot computer unreachable AGAIN — recurring backend failure after multiple repairs","posts_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-05T19:34:13.329Z","views":14,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_p